<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edvard Munch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1863–1944</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edvard Munch (1863–1944) was a Norwegian painter and printmaker and a pioneer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/expressionism">Expressionism</a>. His work dealt with anxiety, love, illness and death, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theme-system">themes</a> drawn from a childhood marked by loss. The Scream (1893), part of his Frieze of Life series, became one of the most famous images in modern art. He left his works to the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edvard-munch.jpg" alt="Edvard Munch" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Edvard_Munch_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
